WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:20,100
My oncologist agreed to write orders for monthly CEAN's CA2729 Tuberbarker lambs.

00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,100
He said, those are the only relevant ones for me.

00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,100
Is that good enough?

00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:33,100
Back when I had active tumors, I ran the CA153 and 199.

00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:38,100
None of them were ever really out of range except for the first 153.

00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,100
And then everything went down after that.

00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:46,100
Well, is that good enough?

00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:50,100
Well, I'd say no.

00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:56,100
I mean, it's better than not running any of them, but especially if this last comment,

00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:02,100
the year 153 was out of range at one point in time or was elevated at one point in time.

00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:05,100
That's going to be probably the one that would be elevated again.

00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:10,100
If, you know, your cancer, you know, came back as active.

00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:15,100
So I would make the argument that this is the one that was elevated before.

00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:17,100
Can you at least run this?

00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,100
I just don't get it.

00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:23,100
Is it any skin off their bones to run that again, you know, good as sinks.

00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:27,100
Here's a person with history and breast cancer.

00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:29,100
Why did they have to be argumentative?

00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:32,100
Why won't insurance pay for two more tests?

00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,100
What's it cost them $20 or something?

00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:38,100
Give me a break. It's just so stupid.

00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:41,100
Yeah, I mean, I'm not knocking you.

00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:45,100
I mean, just do whatever you can, but I would make the argument that this one was out of range before.

00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:49,100
Can you please just run this one again as well?

00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:52,100
So, yeah, it's frustrating.

